{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / RCA\nHapuku change 2852 had two Gerrit Verified failures on the same patchset revision that passed unchanged on retry. Failure evidence:\n\n- run 34281406317 ubuntu lanes failed in `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_sweep_extra_parity_would_have_caught_c57057f41` because the test ran `git show c57057f41:.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` inside a shallow Gerrit patchset checkout where that historical commit was absent.\n- run 34282833154 macOS py3.13 failed the module-size gate with `could not fetch main to verify the module-size limit lock; failing closed`.\n\nThe first class has since been fixed on main by vendoring the historical c57057f41 workflow fixture. The remaining same-class trusted-main fetch defect was the module-size limit lock: a single transient GitHub fetch failure made Verified fail closed even though the absolute module-size cap still ran locally against the patchset tree.\n\n## Plan\n1. Preserve the fail-closed semantics for real module-size limit drift: if trusted main is fetched and `.github/module-size-limit.txt` differs, the gate must still fail.\n2. Make transient trusted-main transport failures deterministic by adding an in-step bounded retry loop to the existing Module-size gate fetch, using the same explicit GitHub URL and existing `refs/remotes/gh-main` destination. The final failed attempt remains fail-closed.\n3. Add RED coverage in `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` that parses the real Module-size gate shell from `_build-and-test.yml` and proves it retries the trusted-main fetch before the existing fail-closed error path.\n4. Keep the existing vendored c57057f41 fixture contract as the regression guard for shallow-checkout historical workflow parity.\n5. Verify with targeted tests and full `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2`, then land through Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `test_sweep_extra_parity_would_have_caught_c57057f41` no longer depends on the historical commit being present in the runner's shallow checkout.\n- [x] The Module-size gate retries transient trusted-main fetch failures before failing closed.\n- [x] The Module-size gate still fails closed if all trusted-main fetch attempts fail.\n- [x] The Module-size gate still fails when the fetched trusted-main limit differs from the patchset limit.\n- [x] The trusted-main fetch continues to use the explicit `https://github.com/${{ github.repository }}` URL, not an assumed `origin` remote.\n- [x] Targeted workflow-parity tests pass.\n- [x] `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes before Gerrit review."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789038182275882001,"uuid":"307c1a18-fdeb-452f-a51f-18471ae82275"}